window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"riven","b":"locke","win":["Riven","Riven","Riven","Riven","Riven","Riven","Riven"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 1","text":"Q auto-cancels already out-trade his auto pressure and dash you clear of the answer."},{"when":"Level 2","text":"Ki Burst stun plus dash mobility locks in your trade pattern — he cannot punish you."},{"when":"Level 3","text":"The full Q-E-W combo out-trades him and your dashes cancel his E dash follow-up."},{"when":"Level 6","text":"Purgatory grounds and slows inside 1000 units — walk out early; Broken Wings will not carry you."}],"wants":{"you":["Q-cancel trades on every single wave","W stun landed before his damage window","All-ins whenever your cooldowns are up"],"foe":["A stationary target for Silver Stake's on-hit","Purgatory landed — it grounds your dashes","Any stage where you fumble the combo"]},"early":"This lane is yours at every stage — play it like it. Q auto-cancels out-trade his Silver Stake pressure from level 1, the level-2 Ki Burst stun locks in your pattern, and the full level-3 Q-E-W combo both out-damages him and cancels his E dash. Trade on every cooldown cycle and stack an early lead.","mid":"Nothing changes at 6 or first item: your shield eats his burst and your dashes deny every all-in — but Purgatory grounds, so when he commits it you walk out of the zone rather than dashing. Watch the Ashen Pursuit wind-up, not the cast; it is a 10s auto reset, and the ten seconds after it are yours.","late":"Late game your Q and R mobility hard-counter the one thing he must do: stick to a squishy target. Duel him freely in the sidelane, hold one dash to break his execute setup, and snowball your lead into splitpush pressure. The only way to lose this is burning every dash before he commits.","whys":["Your level-1 Q auto-cancels let you out-trade his pressure and dash away from the response.","At 2 your early Ki Burst stun and dash mobility keep you firmly ahead in every exchange.","Level 3 your full Q-E-W combo out-trades him and cancels his E dash — trades are yours on demand.","Through 4-5 your shield eats his burst and your dashes deny any all-in he attempts.","At 6 Purgatory grounds you — dashes are off, so leave the zone on foot or above its execute floor.","At first item your shield-heavy burst out-damages his setup window before it completes.","Late your Q and R mobility hard-counter his need to stick a squishy target — the duel stays yours."]});
