window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"riven","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Riven","Riven","Skill","Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 2","text":"Q-W prodding starts winning the short trades before he can build momentum."},{"when":"Level 3","text":"Full Q charges plus the W stun out-burst him — your first genuine kill window."},{"when":"Zaahen levels 4-5","text":"His Q and E come online; if he dodges your W the trades even out — tighten your windows."},{"when":"Your first item","text":"His healing and Determination stacks outscale your burst — trade only on his cooldowns."}],"wants":{"you":["Short combos that end before his answer","The W stun landed to open every all-in","Sidelane duels on your cooldown timers"],"foe":["Extended brawls his passive heals through","Your stun dodged so he can counter-engage","A stat war where his items out-sustain you"]},"early":"Level 1 is even while your combo assembles; from 2 onward the Q-W prod wins the short trades, and level 3 — full Q charges plus the W stun — is your first real kill window, so take it. Respect 4-5: his Q and E come online and even things whenever he dodges your stun, so trade tighter there.","mid":"Six is a mutual kill-button stage: Blade of the Exile can dive through his R, but his all-in punishes any whiffed step just as hard — it is even on paper and decided purely by execution. Your first-item spike breaks the tie: the full combo threatens a real kill, so play it off his cooldown windows.","late":"Late he wins the sidelane duel: Grim Deliverance (110s at rank 1) heals him for part of the damage it deals, his passive revives him at full Determination, and Aureate Rush cuts through armour. Keep Grievous Wounds up, dodge the opening beat of his engage, and split only where your team can rotate to you.","whys":["Level 1 is even — your combo is not assembled yet, so it is a pure skill stage.","At 2 your early Q-W prod starts winning the short trades before he can respond.","Level 3 is your power spike: full charges and the W stun out-burst everything he has.","Even at 4-5: his Q is an auto reset, so react to the wind-up, not the cast.","At 6 both ults are kill buttons — your Blade of the Exile dives through his R, his all-in flips any misstep — so the stage rides on execution.","His Determination stacks and Grim Deliverance heal outpace your first item — buy Grievous Wounds.","Late his revive passive and percent-health E beat your burst — group, do not duel."]});
